# Find-a-Line: append this block to /etc/ufw/after.rules (after its last COMMIT), then
# `sudo ufw reload` (docs/deployment.md, "Firewall"). ufw loads it at boot, before Docker starts;
# Docker never flushes DOCKER-USER, the chain it runs first for traffic forwarded to and from
# containers. Declaring the chain here empties it on every reload, so the rules never pile up.
#
# The containers of Find-a-Line (the bridges br-fal-web and br-fal-worker, named in compose.yaml)
# may reach the internet only: no private, link-local or carrier-grade NAT address (the provider's
# private network, its metadata service at 169.254.169.254, other Docker networks, Tailscale),
# except their own network. Other containers are not affected. Their DNS goes to public resolvers
# (compose.yaml: dns), so a resolver of the provider on a private address is not needed; if
# CONTAINER_DNS_1 is such a resolver, uncomment the two lines with port 53 and put its address there.
*filter
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-web -o br-fal-web -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-worker -o br-fal-worker -j RETURN
#-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 10.0.0.2/32 -p udp --dport 53 -j RETURN
#-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 10.0.0.2/32 -p tcp --dport 53 -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 10.0.0.0/8 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 172.16.0.0/12 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 192.168.0.0/16 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 169.254.0.0/16 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-fal-+ -d 100.64.0.0/10 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -j RETURN
COMMIT
